Subject: [PATCH 1/5] =?UTF-8?q?feat(ai):=20unified=20OpenAI-compatible=20p?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rovider=20=E2=80=94=20switchable=20between=20Z.AI=20and=20Agent?=
 =?UTF-8?q?Router?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Added a new ai-provider.ts module that wraps the standard OpenAI SDK.
This unifies the code path for any OpenAI-compatible gateway:

  - AgentRouter (https://co.agentrouter.org/v1) — set AI_PROVIDER=agentrouter
    + AGENTROUTER_API_KEY. Default model: glm-5.2 (AgentRouter's
    catalog also offers claude-opus-4-8, gpt-5.5, kimi-k2.6, etc.)

  - Z.AI direct (https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4/) — set AI_PROVIDER=zai
    (or leave unset) + ZAI_API_KEY. Default model: glm-4.7-flash (free).

The old z-ai-web-dev-sdk wrapper is kept for backwards compat but no
longer used by the AI routes. The OpenAI SDK handles streaming, retries,
and error mapping consistently across both providers.

Also added per-error-type friendly messages: 401 (auth failed — regenerate
key), 429/1302/1305 (rate limit — wait or upgrade tier), 500/502/503
(transient — will retry). Both routes now return useful content on
provider failure instead of crashing with a generic 500.

Note: user reported their AgentRouter key returned 401 Invalid API Key
during smoke testing. Per AgentRouter docs this is usually because the
key was regenerated since issue. User should generate a fresh key at
https://agentrouter.org/console/token and update AGENTROUTER_API_KEY in
Vercel env vars.
