Base URL: confirmed as https://agentrouter.org/v1 (OpenAI-compatible).
Auth: Bearer token in Authorization header.
Models include:
  - Tier 1 FREE (consume $0 from credit balance): glm-4.5-air, glm-4.6,
    deepseek-v2-lite, qwen2-7b-instruct, mistral-7b-instruct
  - Tier 2-4 paid: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, gpt-4o, deepseek-r1, etc.
  - New sign-ups get $200 free credits via referral link.

Default model switched from glm-5.2 (paid) to glm-4.5-air (FREE on
AgentRouter Tier 1) so the user doesn't burn credits on basic AI calls.

The co.agentrouter.org/v1 endpoint is used (not agentrouter.org/v1)
because the bare domain is behind an Aliyun WAF that blocks non-browser
requests from cloud IPs. Both endpoints accept the same auth + serve
the same models per the docs.

User's API key still returns 401 — they need to regenerate it at
https://agentrouter.org/console/token (the previous key was likely
invalidated when regenerated or the GitHub sign-in wasn't completed).
