After researching all free-tier LLM API options, Google Gemini wins
decisively for our use case:

  Provider    | Free model         | Free rate limit
  ------------+--------------------+----------------------------------------
  Z.AI        | glm-4.7-flash      | ~1 RPM (undocumented, 1302 errors)
  AgentRouter | glm-4.5-air        | Higher (undocumented, key got 401)
  Google ⭐   | gemini-2.0-flash   | 15 RPM / 1M TPM / 1,500 RPD

Gemini's free tier:
  - 15× higher throughput than Z.AI's free tier
  - 1,500 requests per day (resets at midnight Pacific)
  - 1M tokens per minute (practically unlimited)
  - Published, documented, stable limits — no mystery 1302 errors
  - Free forever — no credit card, no expiring credits, no referral link
  - OpenAI-compatible endpoint at
    https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
    Works with the existing OpenAI SDK setup — no code rewrite needed.

Source: https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/rate-limits

Setup (3 env vars in Vercel):
  AI_PROVIDER=gemini
  GEMINI_API_KEY=<free key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey>
  # AI_MODEL is optional — defaults to gemini-2.0-flash

The default AI_PROVIDER is now 'gemini' for new deployments. Existing
deployments that don't set AI_PROVIDER remain on Z.AI for backwards
compatibility — but should switch to gemini for the better rate limits.

Updated the per-provider user-facing error messages: if Gemini returns
401 or 429, the user sees Gemini-specific help (get a free key at
aistudio.google.com/apikey, free tier is 15 RPM / 1,500 RPD, etc.).
